      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70004,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion is confined within the seminal vesicles.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:12:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70005,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most common clinical presentation is obstructive urinary symptoms. Some patients may present with an asymptomatic mass {19660852}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:12:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70006,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fewer than two&nbsp;dozen cases of cystadenoma of the seminal vesicles have been documented since Soule and Dockerty first used the term &ldquo;cystadenoma&rdquo; to describe a &ldquo;pathological curiosity&rdquo; in 1951 {16903949; 19660852; 9610606; 11523949; 30599918; 30511703; 23452815; 14883202; 1593703}. Patient age ranges from 23&nbsp;to 66&nbsp;years.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:12:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70007,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:12:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70008,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:12:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70009,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cystic to solid mass can be as large as 150&nbsp;mm in diameter {19660852; 30599918}. The cut surface is tan-white with cysts of variable size.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:12:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70010,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 321,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Glandular spaces of varying sizes are lined by cuboidal cells without atypia. The glands are arranged in a lobular pattern and form branching lumina and cysts in a scant stroma. The cystic spaces often contain granular intraluminal secretions. Epithelial cells are positive for cytokeratin and negative for PSA, PAP, and calretinin {19660852; 9610606}. Focal luminal AMACR positivity can be seen {30599918}. Stromal cells are weakly positive for SMA and negative for S100.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:12:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
